to determine what Gamma-bar is and see what groups you can have: if I change L and I act on it by O(2), that doesn't change the possibilities for Gamma-bar, it just conjugates Gamma-bar.

27
00:07:10,383 --> 00:07:51,066
所以如果我把 L 换成 A L（A 属于 O(2)），Gamma_bar——我现在先不考虑 Gamma 本身——你得到的只是 O(2) 的同构子群，由正交矩阵共轭的 O(2) 有限子群；并且将 L 乘以一个标量，
So if I change L to A L where A is in O(2), Gamma-bar—I'm not working with Gamma right now—so you get an isomorphic subgroup of O(2), a finite subgroup of O(2) conjugated by an orthogonal matrix; and also changing L to a multiple of L, let's say c · L where c is in R^x,

28
00:07:51,066 --> 00:08:18,021
比如 c · L（c 属于 R^×），也不会改变它，因为如果你取一个点阵 L，把 a 和 b 按相同的标量缩放为 c a 和 c b，那么任何保持原点阵的旋转也必然保持缩放后的点阵，因为旋转与标量矩阵的乘法是对易的。
doesn't change that, because if you take a lattice L and you're scaling a and b out by the same scalar, c a, c b, then any time you have a rotation preserving the lattice, it will preserve this, because rotations commute with multiplication by scalar matrices.

29
00:08:18,021 --> 00:08:20,840
所以这只是对这里的元素进行缩放。
So this just means scaling elements here.

30
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:36,570
因此我真正想要的是：在点阵空间上模掉正交群元素与纯量缩放的作用后来对点阵进行分类。我将在模掉正交群与纯量缩放作用的意义下对所有点阵进行分类：这是一幅著名的数学图景！
So I really want to just classify lattices up to the action on the space of lattices by elements in the orthogonal group and scalars. I'll classify all lattices up to the action of the orthogonal group and scalars: that's a famous mathematical picture!

31
00:08:36,570 --> 00:08:41,240
