00:17:52,660 --> 00:18:10,263
这里围绕原点有六个圆盘，圆盘覆盖了大约 90% 的平面空间，这是在二维空间中以规则方式堆积圆盘最高效的方式，而且早在人类诞生之前蜜蜂就已经发现了这种结构！
There are six circles around the origin here, and it covers about 90% of space with circles, and this is the most efficient way to pack circles in a regular way in two-space, and it's the way that was discovered by the bees long before we were born!

75
00:18:10,263 --> 00:18:18,680
蜜蜂筑成六角蜂巢，如果你想容纳圆形物体并且不想在蜂巢中浪费任何空间，这正是你所需要的。
So you have a honeycomb, and you like to make circular cells and you don't want to waste any space in your hive, this is what you need.

76
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:32,635
好的，这里的另一个特殊点是正方形点阵：这里有四个长度为 1 且互相正交的向量，这就是标准的正方形网格点阵。
Okay, the other nice point here is the square lattice: here there are four vectors of length 1, orthogonal to each other, and that's the standard square lattice.

77
00:18:32,635 --> 00:18:42,136
大家知道，我们有这种标准网格，这是不错的密铺，但不如六角点阵高效。
You know, we have this standard lattice, that's a nice packing, but it's not as efficient as the hexagonal lattice.

78
00:18:42,136 --> 00:19:00,897
而对应于沿着这条边界圆弧的向量的点阵，是包含多个相同长度向量、但夹角不如六角点阵特殊的点阵（菱形点阵）。现在一般的点阵是落在该区域内部的点阵。
And the lattices that correspond to vectors along this boundary line are the lattices where you have vectors of the same length, but not at nice angles like this. Now the general lattice is in the interior of the region.

79
00:19:00,897 --> 00:19:39,200
那么 Gamma_bar 的唯一可能——如果你严格落在内部，不在这个边界点上，也不在这个边界圆弧上，不在边界垂直线上，那么 Gamma_bar 的唯一可能就是 {1} 或C_2，完全正确！
Then the only possibility for Gamma-bar—if you're strictly in the interior, not on this boundary point, not on this boundary circle, not on this boundary line, then the only possibility for Gamma-bar is {1} or C_2, correct!

80
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:46,830
C_2 就是负恒等映射 -I。负恒等映射保持任何点阵，因为它把 a 映为 -a，把 b 映为 -b。
And C_2 just means -I, minus the identity. Minus the identity preserves any lattice, because it takes a to -a and b to -b.

81
00:19:46,830 --> 00:19:55,092
但没有其他旋转能保持该点阵，因为任何旋转都必须把 a 映为与 a 等长的向量。
But there are no other rotations that preserve the lattice, because any rotation would have to take a to a vector of the same length as a.

82
00:19:55,092 --> 00:20:13,072
所以这个群确实就是……抱歉，是的，与 a 等长的向量只有 -a；而且反射也不起作用，除非 b 位于该区域的边界上。
And so this group is really the group... sorry, yeah, the only vector of the same length as a is -a, and reflection doesn't work unless b is on the boundary of this region.

83
00:20:13,072 --> 00:20:44,016
所以如果 b 位于y 轴（虚轴）上，点阵是矩形点阵，那么你可以得到 Gamma_bar 等于 {1}、C_2，而且你还可以有关于水平轴的反射将 b 映为 -b，
So if b is on the y-axis, so your lattice looks rectangular, then you can get Gamma-bar equal to {1}, C_2, but you can also have the reflection across the horizontal line taking b to -b, and likewise across the vertical line taking a to -a;

84
00:20:44,016 --> 00:21:03,224
以及关于垂直轴的反射将 a 映为 -a；而且你还可以有包含这两个正交方向反射的群（克莱因四元群），或者只包含其中一个反射，或者不含反射。
but you can also have the group which contains those two reflections in the two orthogonal directions (Klein 4-group), or it could be a subgroup containing just one of the reflections, or having no reflection.

85
00:21:03,224 --> 00:21:23,083
而在所有这些点阵中，含有额外旋转的点阵只有这两个：对于正方形点阵，我们有 Gamma_bar等于 {1}、C_2，还可以有 4 阶旋转（对应群 C_4 或 D_8）。
And all those lattices that have extra rotations in them are these two lattices: for this lattice (square), we have Gamma-bar equal to {1}, C_2, and there is also rotation of order 4 (C_4 or D_8).

86
00:21:23,083 --> 00:21:37,145
而在六角点阵中，我们可以有 Gamma_bar含有 3 阶旋转（C_3）或 6 阶旋转（C_6 或 D_{12}），旋转 60 度将基向量映回点阵。
And in this lattice, the hexagonal lattice, we can have Gamma-bar having rotations of order 3 (C_3) or order 6 (C_6 or D_{12}), taking this vector back after 60 degrees.

87
00:21:37,145 --> 00:21:43,390
所以这些就是仅有的能得到更大群 Gamma_bar 的两个点阵。
And so these are all the only two lattices in which you can get a larger Gamma-bar.

88
00:21:43,390 --> 00:21:56,054
对吧？哦当然，是 C_4 和 D_8。
Okay? Oh yeah, of course, C_4 and D_8, but not D_4.

89
00:21:56,054 --> 00:22:06,262
好的，这些是矩形点阵中 Gamma_bar 的可能情况，这些是正方形点阵中 Gamma_bar 的可能情况，这些是六角点阵中的可能情况，
Okay, so these are the possibilities for Gamma-bar in the rectangular lattice, these are the possibilities for Gamma-bar in the square lattice, these are the possibilities for Gamma-bar

90
00:22:06,262 --> 00:22:23,893
而这里是一般斜点阵中的可能情况。然后你必须说：好的，如果我有 L 和 Gamma_bar，关于 Gamma 本身我能得出什么结论？
in the hexagonal lattice, and here are the possibilities for the general lattice. Then you have to say: okay, if I have L and I have Gamma-bar, what can I say about Gamma?

91
00:22:23,893 --> 00:22:38,984
因为论证过程完全类似：即我们证明了若点阵中有旋转，其阶数只能是2、3、4 或 6。
Because that's an argument exactly like... exactly: namely, we proved that if we have a rotation in the lattice of order 2, 3, 4, or 6.

92
00:22:38,984 --> 00:22:44,780
好的，对于 1 阶或 2 阶旋转很容易：在任何点阵中，-I 都在 Gamma_bar 中。
Okay, here the rotations of order 1 or 2, that's easy: in any lattice, -I is in Gamma-bar.

93
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:50,319
但如果有一个3 阶旋转，点阵中就必须包含这个特定向量，对吧？
But if we have a rotation of order 3, we have to have this vector in the lattice, right?

94
00:22:50,319 --> 00:23:02,939
已知向量 b 与向量 1，我们就得到这个六角点阵：加 1 就得到点阵中的这个向量，因此如果有 3 阶旋转，我们就已经处于六角点阵的情形了，6 阶旋转亦然。
Given the vector b and the vector 1, we have this hexagonal lattice: if you add 1 to it, you get this vector in the lattice, so we're already in the hexagonal lattice case if you have a rotation of order 3, likewise if you have order 6.

95
00:23:02,939 --> 00:23:10,124
而如果我们有一个4 阶旋转且点阵包含 1，我们就必须在点阵中包含这个向量（i）。
And if we have a rotation of order 4 and we have 1 in the lattice, we must have that this vector is in the lattice.

96
00:23:10,124 --> 00:23:21,765
好的，当我写 1 时，我应该写——我很抱歉，我应该写 (1, 0)；我总写成 1 是因为我把这个平面视作复平面，这正是这一切的奥秘所在！
Okay, when I write 1, I should be writing—I'm sorry, I should be writing (1, 0); I keep writing 1 because I'm thinking of this plane as the complex plane, that's the secret of all this, really!

97
00:23:21,765 --> 00:23:48,121
而且要理解这些，我们用复数代替向量加法，我们可以用复数——很抱歉，我总这样写：我认为这是一个单位根：它确实是，这是迹 2 cos(theta) = -1 的元素，依此类推。
And to do this, we do complex numbers instead of vectors, so we can use complex numbers—I'm sorry, I keep doing this: I think this is a root of unity: it is, and this is the element of trace 2 cos(theta) = -1, and so on, is displayed.

98
00:23:48,121 --> 00:23:58,917
好的，所以这是我们将这里的点阵分类与对所有可能旋转的描述相结合的结果。
Okay, so this is a combination of our classification of lattices here and our description of the possible rotations.

99
00:23:58,917 --> 00:24:07,321
好的，这就结束了这部分，但我向大家保证，随着你们继续深入学习，事实证明这个基本域在数论研究中处于绝对核心的地位！
Okay, that winds up this, but I promise you, as you guys go along and you study mathematics, it turns out that this region is central to the study of number theory!

100
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:19,834
我们真正想知道的是该区域在 R^n 中是什么样子，而我们目前只知道大概直到 8 维的情况，再往上就只有近似估计了。
And what we'd really like to know is what that region looks like in R^n, and we know it all the way up to about eight dimensions, and then it's just approximations.

101
00:24:19,834 --> 00:24:40,306
所以我们非常希望得到 R^n 中所有点阵 Z v_1 + ... +Z v_n 在模掉缩放与 O(n) 意义下的完全分类，天哪，这是现代数学最核心的对象之一！
So we'd very much like to have a classification of all lattices Z v_1 + ... + Z v_n inside R^n up to scaling and O(n), and boy, that's one of the most central objects in modern mathematics!

102
00:24:40,306 --> 00:24:59,237
我们对 n = 2 完全清楚，知道这个区域的长相、它的拓扑结构等等；这在数论中有着重大的应用，所以你们至少应该有所接触。
And we know this for n = 2, you know what this region looks like, what its topology looks like, everything; and this has a major role in number theory, so you should at least be exposed to it.

103
00:24:59,237 --> 00:25:18,807
在 R^n 中，这与球堆积问题密切相关，大家知道我们系里的 Elkies 教授大约五年前取得了重大突破，在更高维空间中构造了极密的高维球堆积。正如我所说，六角密铺是二维空间中已知的最优堆积。
In R^n, this is related to work on sphere packing, and you know that Professor Elkies in the department had a big breakthrough about five years ago, constructing very dense sphere packings in higher-dimensional space. As I said, the hexagonal packing is the best packing in two-dimensional space.

104
00:25:18,807 --> 00:25:28,330
很快就会证明，我们在 8 维和 24 维空间中也找到了最优堆积，分别基于 E_8 格与 Leech 格，这些空间中的球堆积。
It's going to be proved pretty soon that we know the best packings in eight dimensions and in 24-dimensional space, with the Leech lattice and other spaces to pack spheres.

105
00:25:28,330 --> 00:25:33,190
而且由于我们并不知道宇宙的确切维度，这总是有用的！
And since we don't know the dimension of the universe, this will be useful!

106
00:25:33,190 --> 00:25:50,496
即使在三维空间中，也是直到最近才被证明：你在杂货铺水果摊看到的堆法，或者水手堆放炮弹的方式——第一层先排成六角密堆积，然后把炮弹放在那一层的凹坑中，
Even in three dimensions, it was only recently proved that the packing of spheres that you see on grocery stands, where they stack cannonballs by first doing the hexagonal packing in one layer and then stack the balls on the holes of that layer,

107
00:25:50,496 --> 00:25:56,933
再把下一层炮弹放在上一层的凹坑中——这也是你在水果摊看到橙子的堆法——这确实给出了三维空间中最优的球堆积（开普勒猜想）。
and then stack balls on the holes of the next layer—which is also the way you find oranges stacked—that that gives the best—the best packing of spheres in 3-space.

108
00:25:56,933 --> 00:26:01,150
这自 17 世纪以来就被众人所熟知，但一直无人能给出证明！
So that's been known since the 16th century, but nobody proved it!

109
00:26:01,150 --> 00:26:18,402
现在有了一个极其繁复的证明（黑尔斯证明），我对它非常不满意，但它确实是一个证明：它利用计算机分析了成千上万个可能的情况，将其转化为线性规划问题。
Now there is a horrible proof out there, with which I'm very unhappy, but it's a proof: it uses the computer to analyze thousands and thousands of possible cases, turns it into a linear programming problem.

110
00:26:18,402 --> 00:26:31,729
如果能有一个更优美的证明就太好了。无论如何，Elkies 教授提出了这种极其出色的方法，用来确定8 维空间中的最优球堆积。
It would be extremely nice to have a nicer proof. Anyhow, Professor Elkies has got this great method to determine the best packing of spheres in 8-dimensional space.

111
00:26:31,729 --> 00:26:52,292
好的，现在让我介绍一些你们以后会一直用到的语言：研究群 G 的作用——比如R^2 上的刚体运动群 M。现在 R^2 只是一个集合，即点的集合。
Okay, now let me go on with a little bit of language you can use all the time: study the action of the group G—which is the group of motions on R^2. Now R^2 is just a set, the set of points.

112
00:26:52,292 --> 00:27:12,071
现在你可能想研究群在一个一般集合 S 上的群作用：设一般群 G 作用在一般集合 S 上，并为此建立一套语言，因为这在数学中无处不在。
Now you might want to study group actions on a set: let a general group G have an action on a general set S, and develop some language for it, because it comes up all the time.

113
00:27:12,071 --> 00:27:29,977
集合上的一个群作用是指一个从 G x S 到 S 的映射，它将一个元素对 (g, s) 映到元素s 在集合中被映到的像 g · s；它满足两条基本性质：群的恒等元给出集合上的恒等映射，
So a group action on a set is a mapping from G x S to S, which takes an element—a pair (g, s)—to where the element moves s to in the set; and it has two basic properties: the identity of the group is the identity map of the set,

114
00:27:29,977 --> 00:28:02,529
即 e · s = s；并且满足结合律：如果你取g · (h · s)，它等于 (g h) · s。因此当你考察 R^2 上的刚体运动群时，它把向量 s映为向量 A s + b。
so e · s = s; and it's associative: if you take g · (h · s), you find it is (gh) · s. So when you look at this group of motions on R^2, this takes a vector s going to the vector A s + b.

115
00:28:06,993 --> 00:28:24,309
在这里我们也可以考虑群 G 在 R^2 中所有直线 L 的集合上的作用，因为如果你用刚体运动群移动 R^2 中的点，它保持直线，把直线映为直线。
Here we can also take the action of G on the set of lines L in R^2, because if you have points of R^2 moved by the group of motions, it preserves lines, it actually preserves points on the line.

116
00:28:24,309 --> 00:28:53,651
我们再看一个例子：我们也可以考虑 G 在所有三角形集合上的作用，在 R^2 中，因为如果有一个三角形，你有顶点 A 的像、B 的像与 C 的像；这是三个点，边被映为连接它们的新线段，
Let's do another one: or we could take the action of G on the set of triangles in R^2, because if there is a triangle, you get the image of A, the image of B, and the image of C; those are three points, and this one is taken to the line through it, so it goes to another triangle.

117
00:28:53,651 --> 00:29:11,720
所以它变成另一个三角形。在这种情况下，它的不同像都是平面上与原三角形全等的三角形，因为记住，G 保持欧几里得距离，所以三角形的各边长度不变：全等三角形只能映为全等三角形。
In this case, the different images of this are all triangles congruent to that in the plane, because remember, G preserves Euclidean distance, so the distance of sides of the triangle are preserved: congruent triangles go to congruent triangles.

118
00:29:11,720 --> 00:29:38,088
好的，现在给出一些术语：对于集合 S 中的一个元素 s，我们定义两个子集——一个是 S 的子集，称为轨道；另一个是 G 的一个子群 G_s。
Okay, now some terminology: for an element s in S, we define two subsets—one is a subset of S, the orbit; and the other is a subgroup G_s of G.

119
00:29:38,088 --> 00:30:04,508
轨道 O_s 是 G 把 s 能映到的所有点，即形如 s' = g · s（g 属于 G）的点的集合；而稳定子群 G_s 是保持 s 不动的元素构成的子群：
The orbit O_s is all points that G takes s to, so this is the set of s' = g · s for some g in G; and the stabilizer is the subgroup that fixes s: so those things are used all the time for group actions:

120
00:30:04,508 --> 00:30:09,148
这两个概念在群作用中无处不在：对每个点而言，最重要的两件事就是求出其轨道与稳定子群。
the two most important things to do for each point are to find its orbit and to find its stabilizer.

121
00:30:09,148 --> 00:30:33,045
现在让我们看一些轨道与稳定子群的例子。如果我们考虑刚体运动群在平面上的标准作用，原点 0 的轨道是什么？你可以把 0映到哪些点？
Now let's take a look at some orbits and stabilizers. If we take the standard action of this group on the plane, what is the orbit of 0? What points can you take 0 to?

122
00:30:33,045 --> 00:30:42,453
所有点！这里 0 的轨道是整个 R^2，因为任何点都可以通过平移到达：如果我想把 0 映到 b，只需平移向量b。
Everything! The orbit of 0 here is all of R^2, because any point you can translate to: if I want to get 0 to b, I just translate by b.

123
00:30:42,453 --> 00:31:00,639
而 0 的稳定子群是什么？那就是正交群 O(2)：即固定原点的所有线性变换。非零平移都不固定原点，但 O(2) 中的每个元素都固定它。
And what's the stabilizer of 0? That's the group O(2): those are the linear transformations fixing 0. No translation fixes it, but everything in O(2) does.

124
00:31:00,639 --> 00:31:10,600
好的，现在一个非常有趣的问题是：如果我考察这个作用，并固定一条过原点的直线，比如直线 L，
Okay, now a very interesting question is: if I look at this action and I fix a line through the origin, just a line L,

125
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:26,948
这条直线在平面刚体运动群作用下的轨道是什么？这并不难：有人能看出这条直线的轨道是什么吗？在以原点为中心的旋转作用下它的轨道是什么？
what's the orbit of that line under the group of motions of the plane? This is not a hard question: anyone see what the orbit of this line is? What would be the orbit under rotations?

126
00:31:26,948 --> 00:31:34,293
所有过原点的直线，对吧，因为只要绕原点旋转任意角度，你就能到达那里。
Any line through the origin, right, because if I rotate through some fixed angle from the origin, rotating by that you go there.

127
00:31:34,293 --> 00:31:56,099
所以我们得到：L 的轨道 O_L 等于整个直线的集合 S！因为如果外面有任意一条直线，我可以先平移成一条过原点的直线，然后再旋转它。
So we have: the orbit of L, O_L, is equal to S! Because if I have any line out there, I can translate it to a line through the origin, and then rotate it.

128
00:31:56,099 --> 00:31:59,451
因此在这个例子中，你可以把任意一条直线映为任意其他直线。
And so this is a case where you can take any line to any other line.

129
00:31:59,451 --> 00:32:11,412
但在三角形的情形下，我无法把任意三角形映为任意其他三角形，因为如果我有一个这样的三角形，我要把它映为一个那样的三角形，如果它们彼此不全等的话就做不到！
In this case, I can't make every triangle go to every other triangle, because if I have a triangle like this, I'm going to take it into a triangle like that, they're not congruent with each other!

130
00:32:11,412 --> 00:32:13,910
所以这里的轨道正好是所有全等三角形：与给定三角形全等的三角形。这里我不详细证明了。
So the orbit here happens to be the congruent triangles: triangles congruent to that one. I'm not going to prove that.

131
00:32:13,910 --> 00:32:19,879
所以有时轨道是 S 的真子集，有时轨道包含全体元素。
So sometimes the orbit is a subset of S, and sometimes the orbit is all elements.

132
00:32:19,879 --> 00:32:25,629
如果轨道等于整个 S，我们称该群作用是传递的（transitive）。
If the orbit is all of S, we call the action transitive.

133
00:32:37,209 --> 00:32:46,750
这就是关键术语：一个点可以被映到任意其他点，群作用是传递的。所以这个作用是传递作用。
So these are three key terminology points: a point can be taken to any other point, and the action is transitive. So this action is transitive.

134
00:32:46,750 --> 00:33:02,140
O(2) 在点上的作用不是传递的，因为它保持距离：所以如果你仅考虑 O(2) 在平面上的作用，你无法把这个向量映为另一个不同长度的向量，因为必须保持距离不变。
The action of O(2) on points is not transitive, because it preserves distance: so if you have just the action of O(2) on the plane, you couldn't take this vector into that vector of different length, because of distance.

135
00:33:02,140 --> 00:33:04,878
好的，所以某些作用是传递的。
Okay, so some actions are transitive.

136
00:33:04,878 --> 00:33:15,163
现在让我向大家展示一个极其一般的传递作用，它不需要任何几何空间背景：如果你从任意群出发——
Now let me give you a very general transitive action that you don't need a geometric space for: if you start with any group—so this is,

137
00:33:15,163 --> 00:33:53,841
这在某种意义上是传递作用的模型范例：设 G 为任意群，H 为 G 的任意子群，令 S 为左陪集空间 G/H。这是一个极好的集合。
in some sense, the model case of a transitive action: let G be any group, let H be any subgroup of G, and let S be the set of left cosets G/H. That's a perfectly nice set.

138
00:33:53,841 --> 00:34:15,938
G 的作用定义为左平移：它把陪集 aH 映为平移后的陪集 gaH。恒等元保持所有陪集不变，且满足结合律。
The G-action is by left translation: it takes a coset aH to the translated coset gaH. The identity preserves all the cosets, and it's associative.

139
00:34:15,938 --> 00:34:19,690
我断言这是传递的。
I claim this is transitive.

140
00:34:27,530 --> 00:34:32,080
为什么？好吧，我只需找到一个陪集能把它映到任意陪集。
Why? Well, I just have to find one coset that I can send to anything.

141
00:34:32,080 --> 00:34:38,207
如果我取陪集 H，想把它映到陪集 aH，我只需用 a 平移！
And if I take the coset H, and I want to take it to the coset aH, I just translate by a!

142
00:34:38,207 --> 00:35:00,110
通过这个作用你可以从 H 到达任意其他陪集。好的，在这种情况下稳定子群是什么？
And you go from H to any other coset by this action. Okay, what is the stabilizer in this case?

143
00:35:05,940 --> 00:35:19,545
G 中固定陪集 H 的元素集合：也就是满足 gH = H 的 g 的集合，即 H 本身！
The set of elements in G that fixes the coset H: so this is the set of g such that gH = H, which is H itself!

144
00:35:19,545 --> 00:35:55,607
所以如果我想完全从群内部构造一个传递作用，我取任意子群 H，取全体陪集之集 G/H，并通过左平移来定义作用：这是传递的，且 H 的稳定子群就是 H 本身。好的，另一个陪集的稳定子群是什么？
So then if I want to make a transitive action internally from the group, I take any subgroup H, I take the set of all cosets G/H, and define the action by left translation: this is transitive, and the stabilizer of H is H itself. Okay, what is the stabilizer of another coset?

145
00:35:55,607 --> 00:36:16,781
它是满足 g(aH) = aH 的 g 的集合，我断言这就是 a H a^{-1}，对吧？
Well, it's the set of g such that g(aH) = aH, so I claim that this is a H a^{-1}, right?

146
00:36:16,781 --> 00:36:41,230
如果你把它算出来，再次验证即可：这很容易看出来：(a h a^{-1}) a H = a h H = a H，因为 h 属于 H，
If you work this out, again you just check it: it's easy to see: (a h a^{-1}) a H = a h H = a H, because h is in H, so the a and a^{-1} cancel;

147
00:36:41,230 --> 00:36:51,185
a 与 a^{-1} 抵消了；反之，任何固定 aH 的元素都必须属于 a H a^{-1}。所以它是原子群的一个共轭子群！
conversely, anything that fixes aH must belong to a H a^{-1}. So it's a conjugate of the original subgroup!

148
00:36:51,185 --> 00:37:27,767
这在任何传递作用中都成立：更一般地，若 G 传递地作用在 S 上，且我们有 G_s 并想将它与 G_{s'} 进行比较，设 s' = g · s。
And that happens in any transitive action: more generally, if G acts transitively on S, and we have G_s and you want to compare it with G_{s'}, suppose s' = g · s.

149
00:37:27,767 --> 00:37:46,360
于是我们能找到一个把 s 映为 s' 的 g，我们想知道s' 的稳定子群如何用 s 的稳定子群表示：G_{s'} = g G_s g^{-1}。所以稳定子群彼此共轭！
So we find a g that takes s to s', and we want to know what the stabilizer of s' is in terms of the stabilizer of s: G_{s'} = g G_s g^{-1}. So the stabilizers are conjugate!

150
00:37:51,619 --> 00:37:59,848
这是一个简明的论证：大家自己动手算算，一眼就能看出来：假设我有固定 s 的元素，设 h 属于 G_s，
This is an easy argument: you work it out, I just see it: so suppose I have something that stabilizes s, so here's an element h in G_s,

151
00:37:59,848 --> 00:38:11,869
我断言形如 g h g^{-1} 的元素固定 s'：因为 g^{-1} 先把 s' 映为 s；h 固定 s；然后我们再通过 g 映回 s'。
and I claim that an element of this form stabilizes s': well, g^{-1} takes s' to s; and h stabilizes s; then we go back to s' by g.

152
00:38:11,869 --> 00:38:31,788
所以显然这包含在 s' 的稳定子群中；然后你必须证明 s' 稳定子群中的元素用 g^{-1} 共轭后固定 s，这正是完全相同的反向论证。
So it's clear that this is contained in the stabilizer of s'; then you have to show that something in the stabilizer of s', when you conjugate by g^{-1}, stabilizes s, which is the same argument backwards.

153
00:38:31,788 --> 00:38:41,757
事实上，一般传递作用并不比陪集作用更一般：这是我想让大家在本次课中领悟的惊人事实。
In fact, this is really no more general: this is a surprising thing I want you to take out of this lecture.

154
00:38:41,757 --> 00:39:07,480
我们有关于集合上群作用的极其一般的概念；当我们在集合上有一个群作用时，它将集合分解为若干轨道O_s，而在每个轨道上，群的作用都是传递的。所以任何群作用都可以分解为一族传递作用。
So we have this very general notion of a G-action on a set; and when we have a G-action on a set, it breaks the set up into orbits O_s, and on each one of these orbits we have a transitive action. So any action is broken into a bunch of transitive actions.

155
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:14,991
因此关键就在于理解传递作用长什么样；而这里正是一个传递作用的范例：子群的陪集空间上的作用。
So the key is to understand what a transitive action looks like; and here's an example of a transitive action, on the cosets of a subgroup.

156
00:39:14,991 --> 00:40:07,285
一般情形之所以不比这个例子更一般，是因为任何传递作用都同构于子群陪集空间上的群作用：若 G 传递地作用在 S 上，取 s 属于 S 及其稳定子群 G_s，那么在 G-集合S 与陪集空间 G/G_s 之间存在双射。
And the reason that the general case is no more general than this result is that any transitive action is isomorphic to the action on the cosets of a subgroup: if G acts transitively on S, and s is in S with stabilizer G_s, then there is a bijection of G-sets between S and the cosets G/G_s.

157
00:40:07,285 --> 00:40:17,023
G/G_s 与 S 之间建立了双射对应：它取 G/G_s 中的元素g G_s，并将它映为 S 中的元素 g · s。
G/G_s is bijectively identified with S: it takes an element g G_s here and it maps it to the element g · s in S.

158
00:40:17,023 --> 00:40:35,669
大家可以看到，这仅仅依赖于陪集 g G_s，因为如果我将g 乘以一个固定 s 的元素 h，g · s 依然是良定义的，对吧？因为若 h 固定 s，则 (g h) · s = g · (h · s) = g · s。
Now you see that this only depends on the coset g G_s, because if I modify g by an element that fixes s, this element g · s is still well-defined, right? Because if h fixes s, (gh) · s = g · (h · s) = g · s.

159
00:40:35,669 --> 00:40:51,633
所以该映射是良定义的，它只依赖于陪集 g G_s。
So this is well-defined, as it only depends on the coset g G_s.

160
00:40:51,633 --> 00:41:12,763
而且你能通过这种方式得到 S 中的每个元素，所以它是满射，因为群作用是传递的：如果我想得到某个 s'，我总能找到某个把 s 映为 s' 的 g。这是一个传递作用，因此它是满射。
And you get every element in S this way, so it's a surjective map, because the action is transitive: so if I want to get to some s', I find some g that sends s to s'. It's a transitive action, so it's surjective.

161
00:41:12,763 --> 00:41:26,043
并且它也是单射：S 中每个点的原像正好是一个单独的陪集。
And it's also injective: the inverse image of each point here is exactly a coset.

162
00:41:26,043 --> 00:41:47,840
并且该映射与两边的 G 作用相容，因此我们可以把所有传递作用等同于这种陪集作用：一个传递作用确定了一个子群——某个点的稳定子群；而一旦你知道了该子群，你就掌握了这个作用。
And this map is compatible with the G-actions, so that we can identify all transitive actions with this kind of action: a transitive action determines a subgroup—the stabilizer of a point—and once you know that subgroup, you know the action.

163
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:56,656
它确定的并不是唯一的子群，因为为了得到 G_s，我们必须在集合中选取一个点，对吧？
It doesn't determine a unique subgroup, because to get G_s we have to pick a point in the set, right?

164
00:41:56,656 --> 00:42:02,791
如果我们选择集合中的另一个点来定义稳定子群，我们得到的是一个共轭子群。
If we chose a different point in the set to define the stabilizer, we get a conjugate subgroup.

165
00:42:02,791 --> 00:42:16,560
这就是传递作用的真正精髓：传递群作用！
So that's the real moral of transitive actions: transitive actions!

166
00:42:23,390 --> 00:42:40,070
因此每当我们有一个群 G 在集合上的作用时，我们都将其分解为若干轨道，在每个轨道上你都得到一个子群的共轭类，且该轨道等同于在该子群的陪集空间上的作用。
And so every time we have an action of G on a set, we break it into orbits, and on each orbit you get a conjugacy class of subgroups, and the orbit is identified with the action on cosets.

167
00:42:40,070 --> 00:42:48,198
目前为止我们见到的有趣作用还不算太多，但接下来我们将遇到大量极其精彩的作用。
Now so far we haven't had too many interesting actions, but we're going to get a ton of interesting actions coming up.

168
00:42:48,198 --> 00:43:10,119
顺便说一句，如果 G 是有限群且S 是有限集，我们由此可以推导出：G 的阶数等于轨道阶数 |O_s| 乘以稳定子群的阶数 |G_s|！
By the way, if G is a finite group and S is a finite set, we conclude from this that the order of G is equal to |O_s| times the order of G_s!

169
00:43:10,119 --> 00:43:20,880
因为轨道中的元素个数等于指数 [G : G_s]，而我们之前已经证明了子群的阶数乘以其指数等于群 G 的阶数。
Because the number of elements in this set is the index [G : G_s], and we already proved that the order of a subgroup times its index is the order of G.

170
00:43:20,880 --> 00:43:31,055
由此我们得到了一个计数公式！接下来我们将对各种有趣的群作用使用这样的计数公式。
So we get a little counting formula! Now we're going to use counting formulas like this for all kinds of interesting G-actions.

171
00:43:31,055 --> 00:43:40,850
所以也许左平移看起来很简单，但我们可以让 G 作用在自身上，作为一个给出各种计数的精彩作用范例：
So let's say that this left translation might seem simple, but we could have G act on itself as an example of an interesting action giving

172
00:43:40,850 --> 00:44:14,694
G 通过共轭作用在 G 上，g 把 s 映为 g s g^{-1}。其轨道就是共轭类，而 G_s 就是元素 s 在群中的中心化子 Z(s)！
all kinds of counting formulas: G acts on G by conjugation, g takes s to g s g^{-1}. The orbits are conjugacy classes, and G_s is the centralizer of the element s in the group!

173
00:44:14,694 --> 00:44:31,030
因此我们将通过计算中心化子的阶来计算共轭类中的元素个数，我们将使用这类计数公式贯穿我们后续的整个群论部分。
So we're going to count elements in a conjugacy class by calculating what their centralizers are, and we'll be using this kind of counting formula throughout the rest of our group theory.

174
00:44:31,030 --> 00:44:47,362
我们将告别欧几里得刚体运动，进入有限群的抽象理论：计算共轭类、著名的西罗定理（Sylow theorems）、预测特定阶子群的存在性，这大约会占用我们接下来两周的群论学习时间，然后我们才进入环论。
We're going to leave Euclidean motions, and we're going to go into the abstract theory of finite groups: counting conjugacy classes, what are called the Sylow theorems, predicting the existence of subgroups of certain orders, which will take us another two weeks of group theory before we go into rings.

175
00:44:47,362 --> 00:45:01,780
好的，我今天没有展开全部壁纸群的图案；这是一个极其迷人的主题，对化学家尤其重要——不仅是在二维，而且在三维空间中，因为如果你设想三维空间中的同样问题，
Okay, I didn't go into the complete wallpaper designs; this is a fascinating subject, of great interest to chemists, not just in two dimensions but in 3-space, because if you imagine the same problem in 3-space,

176
00:45:01,780 --> 00:45:24,600
寻找在三维正交群O(3) 与平移群下的点阵晶体群，它们描述分子的晶体结构，给出了三维空间中离散刚体运动群（230 个空间群）的完全分类，这让化学家能够弄清晶体是如何形成的。
when you look for lattices under the orthogonal group O(3) and the crystallographic groups that describe forms of molecules, giving a complete classification of discrete motion groups in 3-space, that allows them to figure out how crystals form.

177
00:45:24,600 --> 00:45:35,646
下次课我还会讲一件事：我们可能想对SO(3) 的离散子群进行分类，就像我们对 SO(2) 所做的那样——在 SO(2) 中它们都是循环群，
I will do one more thing next time: we may want to classify the discrete subgroups of SO(3), like we did for SO(2)—in SO(2) they were all cyclic, but in SO(3) you've got some very

178
00:45:35,646 --> 00:45:43,011
但在 SO(3) 中有一些非常有趣的离散群，特别是 A_5：5 个字母上的交错群 A_5 是 SO(3) 的离散子群。
interesting discrete groups, in particular A_5, which you can fit: the alternating group on 5 letters is a discrete subgroup of SO(3).

179
00:45:43,011 --> 00:45:56,784
这个群最近被提出来作为宇宙的可能拓扑模型（庞加莱十二面体空间），这非常迷人，所以我想下次课向大家讲讲 A_5。
And that group has recently been promoted as the model for the universe, which I think is fascinating, so I think I will tell you about A_5 next time.
